WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.040
You need modeling clay that does not harden, bought from a store.

2
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.660
Gather things to press, such as shells, leaves, and a pinecone.

3
00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:12.150
Knead the clay until it is soft.

4
00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:15.070
Flatten it about two centimeters thick on a paper plate.

5
00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:18.630
Press each object straight down, then lift it straight up.

6
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:24.120
Shells with ridges, leaves with thick veins, and toy feet with clear toes make the

7
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.620
sharpest prints. Trade prints and guess what made each one.

8
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.260
Stay with your child the whole time.

9
00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:33.560
If you make plaster casts, only an adult does the plaster.

10
00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:37.700
It can get hot as it hardens, so never press a hand into it.
